NAME
    rsudo-askpass - internal SSH askpass bridge used by rsudo

SYNOPSIS
    rsudo-askpass [prompt...]

DESCRIPTION
    rsudo-askpass is the m-owned helper used by rsudo when SSH requests a
    password through SSH_ASKPASS.

    The command retrieves one password value from the one-shot IPC object named
    by m_RSUDO_ASKPASS_ID and writes that value to standard output followed by a
    newline. Prompt operands supplied by SSH are ignored.

    This is a technical helper for rsudo authentication, not the interface for
    selecting rsudo password acquisition. Use rsudo --askpass for the rsudo
    command mode that consumes a password record from its own standard input.

ENVIRONMENT
    m_RSUDO_ASKPASS_ID
        Required one-shot IPC identifier containing the password value to
        retrieve.

OUTPUT
    On success, standard output carries the retrieved password followed by a
    newline because SSH_ASKPASS consumes the helper's standard output as
    authentication data.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Password retrieval and output succeeded.
    1   m_RSUDO_ASKPASS_ID is absent or the one-shot IPC value cannot be
        retrieved.

    An output failure may also produce a non-zero status.

SECURITY
    Standard output deliberately contains authentication data for SSH. Do not
    invoke or redirect rsudo-askpass as an ordinary user-facing password display
    command.

    The one-shot IPC lifecycle is owned by the rsudo operation that created the
    identifier.

